From: NVX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sched: charge a running task at most a second at once

update_se() charges the running task the task clock's advance since its
last update. A running task's runtime updates at least once a tick, so
the advance is about a tick, unless the task's CPU did not run in
between. A virtual CPU that a snapshot stopped did not: across the
snapshot's downtime, the TSC that sched_clock() reads advances by the
downtime, so the task that ran at the capture is charged the whole
downtime at its first update after the restore.

EEVDF keeps the sum of the queued entities' vruntime keys, each times its
weight, in an s64, and multiplies a key by a weight to decide
eligibility. A nice-0 task's vruntime advances by its runtime, and its
key times its weight overflows an s64 once the advance exceeds
2^63 / 1024 ns, about 104 days, and sooner when heavier entities are
queued with it. After a downtime of a year, pick_eevdf() can then find
no eligible entity, and pick_task_fair() dereferences its NULL result
with the runqueue lock held. The oops kills the task, whose exit
schedules and takes that lock again, so its CPU spins forever.

Charge at most a second of one update: the rest is time in which the
task did not run. Its CPU time and its cgroup's CPU usage then leave the
downtime out, as those of the tasks that did not run at the capture do.

--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1232,6 +1232,17 @@ static s64 update_se(struct rq *rq, struct sched_entity *se)
 	delta_exec = now - se->exec_start;
 	if (unlikely(delta_exec <= 0))
 		return delta_exec;
+
+	/*
+	 * A running task's runtime updates at least once a tick, so a delta
+	 * of more than a second is time in which its CPU did not run, such
+	 * as the downtime of a snapshot, across which the TSC that
+	 * sched_clock() reads advances. Charged, it can overflow the s64 sum
+	 * of EEVDF's weighted vruntime keys, after which pick_eevdf() finds
+	 * no eligible entity.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(delta_exec > NSEC_PER_SEC))
+		delta_exec = NSEC_PER_SEC;
 
 	se->exec_start = now;
 	if (entity_is_task(se)) {
